The opt-in resolution cache restores object fields with cached typed writers, reducing warm materialization work while retaining field-schema validation and the fresh-resolution equality check. Import aliases and export sets with the same qualified name are cached separately, so their dependents can also reuse resolution. Expanded compiler match trees fit the bounded snapshot graph limit, and large equality checks avoid copying full diagnostic path strings for every field. Declarations outside the initial module list retain normal prerequisite misses and uncacheable handling instead of failing a name lookup.
